llama : MoE cache - ClassLRU among the stale slots, the pass rule when a pass overflows

Upstream replaced its SLRU with ClassLRU (#31233, b12283): every expert's uses
decayed with a half-life of 128 tokens (its CRF) rank it in one of eight
classes, one LRU list each, and a miss takes, among the least recently used
slot of each list, the one with the largest age/2^class. The decayed counts
make it better than the SLRU everywhere, and better than EuLLM's former 0008
(the pass and decaying counts, on the SLRU) where a step's experts fit. Where
a step wants more experts than there are slots it still evicts slots used
within the pass: the oldest slot of a high class can score below a recent slot
of class 0, the one holding an expert the next layers are about to select
again, since the layers come in the same order every step. Replayed through
bench/moe_cache_sim (EuLLM) on routing calibrated to LUMI-G it found 65.9% of
the experts in VRAM for Qwen3-235B with 32 sequences where the former 0008
found 73.1%, and 0% for Qwen3-Coder-480B with 32 where it found 21.1%.

This patch keeps ClassLRU and adds the pass to it. The victim is ClassLRU's,
chosen among the stale slots only, those whose expert was not selected during
the last pass over the layers of the group. When every slot was used within
the last pass, the miss takes, among the slots used earlier in this pass, the
one with the lowest decayed CRF (the most recently used before this layer's
own if there is none), whose expert is selected again a whole pass later at
the earliest. A recency list of all the slots and the plan of each slot's last
use say which are stale and which were used in this pass. While a pass fits,
a stale slot always exists and the victim is ClassLRU's. Replayed: ClassLRU's
hits where a step fits, and at or above the former 0008 where it overflows
(235B with 32: 73.2%; 480B with 8: 46.8%, with 32: 21.8%), over ten more
settings of the routing at most 0.17 points below it, once.
LLAMA_MOE_CACHE_EVICT=classlru evicts by ClassLRU alone, to compare.

Upstream now writes LLAMA_MOE_CACHE_TRACE itself ("MCT1", every group of
layers), which bench/moe_cache_sim reads; the former 0008's own trace
("MOEC", the first group only) is gone.

Statistics: LLAMA_MOE_CACHE_STATS=N counts every step that went through the
cache (32 tokens or fewer), not only those of up to 8, and says which share
of the copies went into a slot used within the pass; the totals at exit count
those misses too.

EuLLM patch on llama.cpp b12283, after 0002 (which adds the statistics).

